course: dictionary
lesson: 10738
title: Upsetting words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Upsetting means making you feel sad, worried or unhappy. Usually it describes something that happens or something you see or hear: «Watching a game being played can be just as frightening or upsetting as playing it yourself.» The film, game or news is the thing that makes you feel bad.
explain: The verb upset works the other way round. Upsetting someone means making them feel sad or worried. «If you see something upsetting or someone is mean to you, do not reply; tell a trusted adult.» The clue here is what you should do when something makes you feel bad.
explain: Upsetting has other meanings too: knocking something over, spoiling a plan, or having an upset stomach when you feel ill. Look at the words around it to decide which one fits, then swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: Upsetting is an adjective when it describes a thing: upsetting news, an upsetting film.
fact: The forms are upsetting, more upsetting and most upsetting.
fact: As a verb, upset means making someone feel sad or worried, or knocking something over.
fact: «Upset stomach» means your tummy feels ill.
fact: If something online is upsetting, tell a trusted adult, and you will not be in trouble for telling.
exercise: «An accident is something nobody meant to happen; grown-ups can explain what happened simply, without upsetting details.» What does upsetting mean here? | Details that are loud | *Details that make you feel sad or worried | Details that are neat and tidy | Details that are very long
exercise: Mia's drink spilt because her friend upset the cup. What does upset mean here? | Ran very fast | *Knocked something over | Felt very happy | Told a secret
exercise: Tom says, «I have an upset stomach after lunch.» What does he mean? | He is very angry with his lunch | He ate too much cake and is full | He has a new lunchbox | *He feels ill in his tummy
test: «Bots sometimes say upsetting things despite safety rules; close the app and tell a grown-up.» What should you do? | Keep chatting to the bot to see what it says next | Reply rudely to the bot | *Close the app and tell a grown-up | Share the message with everyone
test: The news was very ___, so I asked my mum for a hug. | *upsetting | upsetly | upsets | upsetter
exam: If you see something upsetting online, what should you do first? | Reply to the person who sent it | Keep it secret so nobody knows | *Tell a trusted adult | Share it with your friends so they can see
